{
  // F2's code-quality audit deepened each wave and its runtime grew with it:
  // 50m, then 1h15m, then 2h49m — at which point the default 90-minute
  // stale-timeout cancelled it mid-audit with no report, leaving the fourth
  // wave with only three of four verdicts.
  //
  // F2 is the only reviewer that works by production mutation, and it found a
  // real defect in every wave it completed (a toy channel standing in for a
  // production one, guards asserting the parse instead of the dispatcher, a
  // permission surface with no production bridge, an expiry test passing for
  // the wrong reason). Cutting its scope to fit a timeout would trade the
  // project's best defect-finder for a faster green light.
  //
  // Raised to 4 hours so a deep audit can finish. Applies to every background
  // task; the memory gate (~100 min) and the soak (2 h) also sit under it.
  "background_task": {
    "staleTimeoutMs": 14400000
  }
}
